[75.2663, "o", "\u001b[38;5;82mdiscovery: done\u001b[m\r\n"]
[75.2995, "o", "\r\n[history] Neuromancer — William Gibson\r\nA foundational cyberpunk novel that explores AI and programming in a visionary future.\r\n\r\n[interests] Artificial Intelligence: A Guide to Intelligent Systems — Michael Negnevitsky\r\nThis book offers a comprehensive overview of AI concepts and applications, making it an excellent resource for understanding the technology driving modern developments.\r\n\r\n"]
[75.2995, "o", "[discovery] Sapiens: A Brief History of Humankind — Yuval Noah Harari\r\nThis book provides a deep overview of human history, connecting our biological evolution to technological advancements—bridging a gap between humanities and the technological themes in your interests.\r\n\r\n[history] The Pragmatic Programmer — Andrew Hunt and David Thomas\r\nAn essential read for all programmers, offering practical advice and insights.\r\n\r\n[interests] Clean Code: A Handbook of Agile Software Craftsmanship — Robert C. Martin\r\nThis book emphasizes writing clean, efficient code—essential for anyone serious about programming, particularly in AI where maintainability is key.\r\n\r\n[discovery] The Hidden Life of Trees: What They Feel, How They Communicate — Peter Wohlleben\r\nExploring the intricate relationships within forest ecosystems can surprise you by showing how interconnectivity in nature parallels programming concepts, like networks and systems.\r\n"]
[75.3382, "o", "\u001b[?2026$p\u001b[?2027$p"]
